release lights sooner. Commit writes ALL-TESTS.md from the tests (tools/all_tests.py) before it adds the changes.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 21:04:48

Added. An orange banner above the release's steps while the wiki's Portal Tour is older than the portal (its window
or its tiles; tools/portal_tour.py --check), with Record new video now, which records it on the Commands tab
(tools/record-tour.sh --wiki). Start new release stays off until the video is recorded, and checks once more before
it writes the release; a check that cannot run holds the release too.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 10:17:45

Breaking. One suite (owner, 15-11-2026): the code for several suites in one repository is gone (the Portals column,
the suite chosen in the settings, Nexus's own version and its nexus-v tags, the other suites' workflows). The
release is release.yml's, the ticker and the notifications show every run of the push, and the commit runs
tools/check_versions.py and tools/check_manifest.py once. has_release_workflow(), unused since the manual mode went,
is gone too.

Breaking. No VERSION (owner, 15-11-2026): a development app is never released, so its header names the checkout's
last commit and its time ("5fb1aa8 · 15-11-2026 07:20", core's nexus.header()) where it showed a version, and
--version prints the same.

Fixed. The app imports bazzite_console_core directly, with the Nexus design from core's nexus.py (owner,
15-11-2026): the compatibility package dev/core_compat is gone, and run.sh puts only core/ on the path.

Fixed. An open incident on githubstatus.com counts as GitHub being down, with its stage (monitoring) in its name:
the page's indicator goes back to none while an incident is still being monitored. Commit offers the portal bump
when apps.toml changed since the last portal release. The Remove suite text names check-release.sh remove --purge
again.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 08:41:40

Fixed. Publish fetches main with the new tag (owner, 15-11-2026), so Bring in the pin commit lights as soon as it
ends: the pin commit, pushed with the workflow's token, has no run of its own on main, and the steps showed every
step done while it was not pulled yet. The steps follow only a release run on main, never one on a tag.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 07:50:10

Fixed. Right after a push, the GitHub pill and the line under the pills wait for GitHub to start the runs of the
commit pushed (owner, 15-11-2026): until then they showed the runs of the commit before, so a push after a commit
that failed showed as failed, then as passed. While Run CI again runs, its step says so.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 07:21:45

Fixed. Push shows where CI's jobs here stand (owner, 15-11-2026: the push seemed to hang, and a job that failed went
unseen while the line under the pills showed the last push on GitHub as passed): while tools/ci-local.sh runs, the
step's line and the line under the pills count the jobs done and name a job that failed, and say when the run waits
for another one. A push that ended badly turns the step red with why (the jobs that failed, where their logs are,
or a stop), until the commit is pushed or HEAD changes. Run CI again, and the Run again of that line, stay off for
the runs they were pressed for until GitHub shows them running again: until then GitHub still showed them failed,
and a second press failed with "This workflow is already running".

Changelog: 15-11-2026 06:09:24

Fixed. A part whose only changes since its last tag are its version, its version copies and a "Release x.y.z."
entry (or Retract's "Withdrawn:" entry) needs no release any more: Start new release left it out. A portal bump
with nothing else in it was released as a second portal of the same apps, waiting for a device test of its own, and
a withdrawn app was released again with its withdrawal (owner, 15-11-2026).

Changelog: 15-11-2026 06:09:24

Breaking. The release by hand is gone (owner, 15-11-2026): the tabs 1. Release apps (with the header's Apply),
2. Pin and release Portal (Pin, Bump portal, Fetch tags), their Publish buttons, the tab Test on this board and the
release tab's mode for a repository without a release workflow, which pointed to those tabs. Their Bump wrote a
portal release while the release tab's draft waited for its device test, which then went out as a second release.
The release tab's Start new release writes everything a release needs, and its Device test tests the draft. Test
withdrawal is on the tab Retract app now (no longer numbered), whose last step is a release from the release tab;
Remove suite has a tab of its own. tools/tag-release.sh still builds and publishes a single release from a
terminal.

